        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "VCC : C1.1(passive) J5.2(Pin_2,passive) JP1.2(B,passive) Q1.2(S,passive) R1.1(passive) R6.1(passive) U1.3(VI,power_in)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "R1 VCC Net-_Q1-G_ 10"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "When the MCU PWM signal turns Q2 on, R1 forms a low-resistance path from VCC through Q2 to ground. Depending on VCC, this can draw hundreds of milliamps or more continuously, overloading the 0805 resistor and BC817 transistor, causing heating or damage and potentially pulling down the VCC rail.",
      "confidence": 0.97
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design is mostly consistent, but R1 is a 10-ohm pull-up in the P-MOSFET gate drive instead of a high-value pull-up such as 10 kΩ. This creates a large continuous current path through R1 and Q2 when Q2 is on."
}

